    id: 'blog-40',
    title: 'Off-Season Sourcing Is Booming: Why Smart Sweater Buyers Order in Summer',
    excerpt: 'While shoppers buy swimwear, smart manufacturers are filling fall orders. Inside the off-season order wave and how early ordering wins capacity, price and quality.',
    content: 'It is 35°C outside, and the hottest topic in China\'s knitwear towns is... sweaters. As CCTV reported in August 2026, off-season orders for winter products are booming across China\'s apparel clusters — manufacturers of sweaters, gloves and winter gear are racing to fulfill "reverse-season" orders placed months ahead of cold weather. For international buyers, this is the single best window to lock in capacity, prices and quality.\n\n## Why off-season ordering works\n\nOrdering fall/winter knitwear in summer is not just about being organized — it delivers concrete advantages:\n\n- **Factory capacity**: machine time is available, so lead times shorten and schedules are reliable.\n- **Price leverage**: with demand low, factories are more flexible on pricing and MOQs.\n- **Sample cycles**: there is room to iterate samples without rushing, which improves fit and finish.\n- **Shipping windows**: production finishing in late summer avoids the pre-holiday freight rush and its surcharges.\n\n## The reverse-season wave by the numbers\n\n| Signal | What it shows |\n|--------|---------------|\n| CCTV reverse-season report (Aug 2026) | Winter-product clusters at full capacity in summer |\n| Dalang cluster output | Production begins for AW26 programs months early |\n| Freight markets | Off-peak booking = lower rates and faster transit |\n| Factory pricing | Off-season quotes typically 5-15% below peak-season pressure |\n\n## A practical timeline for AW26 (and beyond)\n\n| Month | Action |\n|-------|--------|\n| Jan-Mar | Review sell-through data, define next season\'s brief |\n| Apr-Jun | Send yarn/color directions, book sample slots |\n| Jul-Aug | Finalize samples, place bulk orders (off-season window) |\n| Sep-Oct | Production and inspection; begin shipping |\n| Nov-Dec | Deliveries land before peak demand; reorder fast-movers |\n\n## What to prepare before you order in summer\n\n1. **A clear spec sheet** — fibre/blend, gauge, neckline, sizes, colors. Factories quote faster and more accurately with a full brief.\n2. **Reference samples** — photographs, swatches or a physical garment to match.\n3. **Certification requirements** — Oeko-Tex, BSCI/Sedex, or retail-specific compliance.\n4. **A realistic MOQ** — and a backup style if your volume is small (ODM options help here).\n\nWorking with a Dalang-based manufacturer such as LINFAIR during the off-season window means your AW26 program gets dedicated machine time, faster samples and a calmer, more attentive production run — before the September rush begins.\n\n## FAQ\n\n**Is it really cheaper to order sweaters in summer?**\nOften yes — off-season demand softens pricing and avoids peak freight surcharges. Savings of 5-15% are realistic.\n\n**Won\'t factories be idle and slow in summer?**\nNo — the reverse-season wave means capable factories are busy with forward orders, which is exactly why booking early secures capacity.\n\n**How early is too early?**\nSamples 4-6 months ahead and bulk orders 2-3 months ahead is a healthy rhythm; anything earlier risks missing trend shifts.\n\n## Sources\n\n- CCTV News, "Off-season orders boom; traditional industry upgrades with smart manufacturing" (Aug 2026)\n- CNR (央广网), Dalang sweater export coverage (Aug 2026)\n- China Textile News, wool industry market reports (2026)',
